# Docker build context trimming.
#
# Dockerfile.k8s, Dockerfile.runner and Dockerfile.services COPY only the booking_* packages,
# plus `attack` and k8s/v5/init-data for the services image. The recorded results add about a
# thousand files to the context for no reason, which is slow over the macOS file-sharing layer
# and slower still when the context is streamed to a docker-in-docker daemon.
#
# The results and the cache directories are read by no COPY. Backups of earlier states
# (`*.pre-*`, `*.bak`) must not reach an image, because they would sit inside a copied package.
results/
results_v1_2/
results_v2/
results_v2_1/
results_v3/
results_v4_container/
results_v4_controller/
results_v4_durable/
results_v4_k8s/
results_v4_process/
results_v5/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.git/
.DS_Store

# Backups of earlier states must not travel inside a copied package.
**/*.pre-*
**/*.bak
